     I've never heard of hack121, but the way to level teleport
in ancient versions of hack was to read a scroll of teleportation
while confused (which continues to work in nethack, but is no
longer a required action).  I can't remember if rings of teleport
control existed back then or whether there was any other way to
let you specify the destination.

     I played pchack 20 years ago and got stuck at the same point
because I didn't know about that teleport trick.  I was able to
get down as far as the third maze level by repeatedly entering a
trapdoor on the bottom non-maze level, but wrongly concluded that
existence of the Amulet of Yendor was a cruel hoax and eventually
gave up.  (There wasn't anything called a Sphere of Power, but
there was a wand of wishing hidden underneath a boulder.  I don't
remember whether that was on every maze level or just the first.)


